# ── Served-data exposure (2026-07-03) ────────────────────────────────────────
# Raw vendor fields must not be published (ToS). These files are regenerated by
# the pipeline and kept in the LOCAL working tree only; `git rm --cached` removes
# them from the index and these patterns stop CI `git add data/markets/` from
# re-introducing them. NB: gitignore is INERT on an already-tracked file, so the
# `git rm --cached` is what actually stops publication. robotnik_public_markets.json
# was listed here on 2026-07-03 but stayed tracked (and served) until the untrack
# finally landed 2026-08-22 — see the block below.
data/markets/robotnik_public_markets.json
data/markets/enriched_equities.json

# ── Served-data exposure: raw vendor price substrate (2026-08-22) ─────────────
# Completes the served-data close-out. Raw MarketStack / Yahoo / CoinGecko fields
# (price, change_pct, volume, market_cap, sparkline, and the 5-year OHLC history
# store) must not be published (vendor ToS + Robotnik served-data rule). Every file
# here is regenerated in the working tree on each pipeline run; the history store
# and market caps additionally persist across CI runs via actions/cache (see
# .github/workflows/fetch-data.yml), NOT the git tree. `git rm --cached` removed
# them from the index; these patterns stop CI `git add` from re-introducing them.
data/prices/equities.json
data/prices/all_prices.json
data/prices/tokens.json
data/prices/benchmarks.json
data/prices/history/
data/index/market_caps.json
data/markets/marketstack_coverage_report.json
data/markets/marketstack_coverage_report.md
data/markets/coverage_report.json
